---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Why Flash Was Actually Great | Articles">
  <article class="article-page">
    <header class="article-header">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="back-link">← Back to Articles</a>
      <h1 class="page-title">Why Flash Was Actually Great</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>📅 January 15, 2024</span>
        <span>⏱️ 5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body content-box">
      <p>
        Let's talk about something that's been on my mind lately: <strong>Macromedia Flash</strong>.
        Yes, that Flash. The one that got killed off, blamed for security holes, and replaced
        by HTML5. But here's the thing — Flash was actually incredible.
      </p>

      <h2>The Creative Explosion</h2>
      <p>
        In the early 2000s, Flash was everywhere. Band websites had elaborate animated intros.
        Games like <em>QWOP</em> and <em>Line Rider</em> captured millions of hours of our time.
        Homestar Runner became a cultural phenomenon. Newgrounds was the YouTube before YouTube.
      </p>

      <p>
        Flash democratized animation and interactive content. Anyone with a copy of Flash MX
        could create something magical. You didn't need to know complex programming — the
        timeline-based animation was intuitive and visual.
      </p>

      <h2>The Web Had Personality</h2>
      <p>
        This is what I miss most. Flash websites had <em>character</em>. Each site was a unique
        experience. You'd wait for the loading bar to fill up, then be transported to someone's
        creative vision. Sounds would play. Things would animate. It felt alive.
      </p>

      <div class="quote-box">
        "The web used to be weird, and that was beautiful."
      </div>

      <p>
        Compare that to today's web: endless scrolling feeds, cookie banners, the same Bootstrap
        layouts everywhere. We gained performance and accessibility, but lost a lot of soul.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Can Learn</h2>
      <p>
        I'm not saying we should bring Flash back (please don't). But we <em>can</em> bring
        back the spirit:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Add meaningful animations that delight users</li>
        <li>Design unique experiences, not templates</li>
        <li>Include easter eggs and surprises</li>
        <li>Let your personality shine through</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This website is my attempt at capturing that magic with modern tech. GSAP gives us
        the animation power. CSS lets us create wild visual effects. The tools have never
        been better — we just need to use them creatively.
      </p>

      <p>
        Long live the spirit of Flash. ⚡
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="nav-btn">← More Articles</a>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <style>
    .article-page {
      max-width: 750px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .article-header {
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-terminal);
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .article-body {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .article-body h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-tech);
      font-size: 20px;
      color: var(--color-secondary);
      margin: 30px 0 15px;
      padding-left: 15px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--color-secondary);
    }

    .article-body p {
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      color: #ccc;
    }

    .article-body strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-body em {
      color: var(--color-accent);
      font-style: normal;
    }

    .article-body ul {
      margin: 20px 0;
      padding-left: 30px;
    }

    .article-body li {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      color: #bbb;
    }

    .article-body li::marker {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .quote-box {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 0, 255, 0.1), transparent);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--color-secondary);
      padding: 20px;
      margin: 25px 0;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 18px;
    }

    .article-footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid #333;
      text-align: center;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
